WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.048
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Writing Skills.

2
00:00:05.348 --> 00:00:08.874
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.174 --> 00:00:15.263
Unit three: Writing a Paragraph. Today you will write a paragraph with a clear topic sentence.

4
00:00:15.563 --> 00:00:18.273
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.233 --> 00:00:22.455
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.317 --> 00:00:24.434
Paragraph.

7
00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:28.808
Paragraph means a group of sentences about one idea.

8
00:00:29.417 --> 00:00:30.824
Write one paragraph.

9
00:00:31.417 --> 00:00:34.173
Your turn. Say: Paragraph.

10
00:00:37.033 --> 00:00:38.058
Paragraph.

11
00:00:38.817 --> 00:00:40.131
Topic sentence.

12
00:00:41.117 --> 00:00:44.498
Topic sentence means the sentence that gives the main idea.

13
00:00:45.083 --> 00:00:47.153
Start with a topic sentence.

14
00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:50.820
Your turn. Say: Topic sentence.

15
00:00:53.667 --> 00:00:54.993
Topic sentence.

16
00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:56.670
Supporting.

17
00:00:57.683 --> 00:01:00.194
Supporting means helping to prove an idea.

18
00:01:00.783 --> 00:01:02.377
Add supporting details.

19
00:01:02.983 --> 00:01:05.415
Your turn. Say: Supporting.

20
00:01:08.267 --> 00:01:09.198
Supporting.

21
00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:10.951
Detail.

22
00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:14.565
Detail means a small piece of information.

23
00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:16.604
Add one more detail.

24
00:01:17.217 --> 00:01:20.043
Your turn. Say: Detail.

25
00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:23.762
Detail.

26
00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:25.553
Example.

27
00:01:26.550 --> 00:01:29.095
Example means a case that shows an idea.

28
00:01:29.683 --> 00:01:30.835
Give an example.

29
00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:33.986
Your turn. Say: Example.

30
00:01:36.833 --> 00:01:37.695
Example.

31
00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:39.463
Concluding.

32
00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:42.519
Concluding means ending or finishing.

33
00:01:43.117 --> 00:01:44.861
Write a concluding sentence.

34
00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:48.300
Your turn. Say: Concluding.

35
00:01:51.133 --> 00:01:52.297
Concluding.

36
00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:54.005
Unity.

37
00:01:55.017 --> 00:01:57.771
Unity means having one main idea only.

38
00:01:58.383 --> 00:02:00.058
A paragraph needs unity.

39
00:02:00.650 --> 00:02:02.966
Your turn. Say: Unity.

40
00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:06.580
Unity.

41
00:02:07.317 --> 00:02:08.295
Indent.

42
00:02:09.283 --> 00:02:11.852
Indent means to start a line further in.

43
00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:13.985
Indent the first line.

44
00:02:14.583 --> 00:02:17.375
Your turn. Say: Indent.

45
00:02:20.233 --> 00:02:21.258
Indent.

46
00:02:22.067 --> 00:02:25.717
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:26.583 --> 00:02:28.653
Visal, how do I build a paragraph?

48
00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:38.732
Start with a topic sentence. Then add two or three supporting sentences with details and examples. Finish with a concluding sentence.

49
00:02:39.817 --> 00:02:41.178
How long should it be?

50
00:02:42.283 --> 00:02:47.922
Usually five to eight sentences. Write about one idea only. This is called unity.

51
00:02:49.017 --> 00:02:50.738
What is a topic sentence?

52
00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:58.810
It tells the reader the main idea of the paragraph. For example, Reading every day improves your vocabulary.

53
00:02:59.967 --> 00:03:01.432
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:02.283 --> 00:03:05.142
Grammar focus: Paragraph structure.

55
00:03:05.442 --> 00:03:06.652
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:07.350 --> 00:03:13.523
Reading improves vocabulary. You meet new words in every text. So reading is a useful habit.

57
00:03:14.417 --> 00:03:19.591
Exercise is healthy. It makes the heart strong. Therefore, exercise daily.

58
00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:27.084
Write one main idea in the topic sentence, support it with details and examples, and finish with a concluding sentence.

59
00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:32.400
Be careful! Don't say: Reading is good. And fun. And cheap.

60
00:03:34.367 --> 00:03:36.900
Say: Reading is good, fun and cheap.

61
00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:38.898
Keep one clear sentence.

62
00:03:39.700 --> 00:03:42.538
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:43.333 --> 00:03:44.892
My Study Paragraph.

64
00:03:45.192 --> 00:03:48.027
Rina writes a paragraph about study habits.

65
00:03:49.033 --> 00:03:52.229
Her topic sentence says that daily study is important.

66
00:03:53.233 --> 00:03:55.744
She adds two details and one example.

67
00:03:56.733 --> 00:03:58.744
She writes only about one idea.

68
00:03:59.733 --> 00:04:02.267
Her last sentence repeats the main idea.

69
00:04:03.367 --> 00:04:07.194
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:08.050 --> 00:04:10.328
A paragraph has one blank idea.

71
00:04:10.628 --> 00:04:13.852
A, main. B, blue. C, loud.

72
00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:19.063
The answer is A: main.

73
00:04:20.217 --> 00:04:22.808
The first sentence is the blank sentence.

74
00:04:23.108 --> 00:04:26.379
A, long. B, topic. C, last.

75
00:04:29.933 --> 00:04:31.503
The answer is B: topic.

76
00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:34.603
Details blank the main idea.

77
00:04:34.903 --> 00:04:38.452
A, stop. B, hide. C, support.

78
00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:44.371
The answer is C: support.

79
00:04:45.517 --> 00:04:47.714
The last sentence is the blank sentence.

80
00:04:48.014 --> 00:04:51.412
A, concluding. B, opening. C, middle.

81
00:04:54.967 --> 00:04:56.966
The answer is A: concluding.

82
00:04:58.117 --> 00:05:00.232
Rina writes about blank idea.

83
00:05:00.532 --> 00:05:03.118
A, no. B, one. C, ten.

84
00:05:06.667 --> 00:05:08.399
The answer is B: one.

85
00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:13.019
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:13.883 --> 00:05:15.581
How do you write a paragraph?

87
00:05:24.383 --> 00:05:25.849
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:26.149 --> 00:05:37.163
I begin with a topic sentence that gives the main idea. Then I add details and an example. I write about one idea only and finish with a concluding sentence.

89
00:05:37.463 --> 00:05:39.161
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:40.050 --> 00:05:43.968
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and paragraph structure.

91
00:05:44.268 --> 00:05:49.184
Today's value is discipline. Follow your routine, even when it is hard.

92
00:05:49.484 --> 00:05:52.020
See you in Unit four. Goodbye!

93
00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:55.762
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

